{"name":"Sierra Foothills","hex":"#a28a67","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sierra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Sierra of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rugged range of mountains.","Alternative letter-case form of Sierra from the NATO/ICAO Phonetic Alphabet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sierra"},{"term":"foothills","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of foothill"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foothills"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sierra Foothills AVA","blocks":[{"text":"Sierra Foothills is a vast American Viticultural Area (AVA) encompassing portions of seven of the twelve California counties in the foothill \"belt\" of the Sierra Nevadas in north-central California, an interior range that extends about 360 mi (580 km) in a northwest–southeast orientation from Mt. Lassen to Walker Pass near Bakersfield. The viticultural area is approximately 160 mi (260 km) long and lies 40 mi (64 km) to the east of Sacramento."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Sierra_Foothills_AVA_location_on_TTB_Map.png/330px-Sierra_Foothills_AVA_location_on_TTB_Map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sierra_Foothills_AVA","wikidata":"Q1646258"},{"title":"Foothills","blocks":[{"text":"Foothills or piedmont are geographically defined as gradual increases in elevation at the base of a mountain range, higher hill range or an upland area. They are a transition zone between plains and low relief hills and the adjacent topographically higher mountains, hills, and uplands. Frequently foothills consist of alluvial fans, coalesced alluvial fans, and dissected plateaus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Foothillsco.JPG/330px-Foothillsco.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foothills","wikidata":"Q1354045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Sierra_Foothills_Vineyard_0001.jpg/500px-Sierra_Foothills_Vineyard_0001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Sierra_Foothills_Vineyard_0001.jpg/500px-Sierra_Foothills_Vineyard_0001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vineyards near Vallecito, California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASierra_Foothills_Vineyard_0001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Prospect_Hill.jpg/500px-Prospect_Hill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Prospect_Hill.jpg/1280px-Prospect_Hill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Prospect_Hill.jpg/500px-Prospect_Hill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Foothills of Prospect Hill, New South Wales, Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProspect_Hill.jpg"}],"sounds":{"sierra":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-sierra.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-sierra.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-sierra.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-sierra.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-sierra.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/29/En-us-sierr